{"text": "- - \u2018July 10, 1987\n\nTo: Yen Ke Le Verner\nMEAL G. Linville :\nFROM: Jack Bellis\nSUBJECT: ACCEPTANCE FOR SALEM LIGHTS aS VERSUS CAMBRIDGE LIGHTS M85 ,\n\nA Product Test report was recently issued by MDD addressing product\nperformance for Savings 20's brands versus full price brands. This report\nindicated that Cambridge Lights M85 was superior to SALEM Lights 85 anong 18+\nSALEM Lights 85 franchise snokers. Although this may be the case, the degree\nOf difference in acceptance between SALBM and Canbridge was overstated due to\na typo \u2014 acceptance for SALEM (through Wave I, 1987) was reported to be 52,\nwhen it should_have been a 62. Further, the latest competitive results for\nSALEM Lights 85 anong franchise (through Wave II, 1987) shows SALEM receiving\nan acceptance score of 68 which would place it at parity to Caubridge.\n\n270+ Acceptance\n\nConbridge Lights 4 85 ne\nSALEM Lights 85 (ehrough W2, 67) 68\nSALEM Lights 85 (through WL, 87) 6 \u2014\n\n*This improvement was also reflected in attribute results.\n\nAlthough current franchise acceptance for SALEM places it at parity to\nCambridge, it is doubtful that SALEM can maintain franchise acceptance ia the\nhigh 60's. From first quarter, 1986 through first quarter, 1987 (five waves\nof testing), franchise acceptance for SALEM ranged from 60-65.\n\nAccordingly, SALEM could well be inferior to Cambridge on average and over\ntine. However, SALEM Brand Research does not recommend further testing of\nCanbrfdge. R&D has an aggressive product inprovenent plan ia place that will\nresult in NFO prototypes during third quarter. Further, the attribute\nadvantages that Cambridge has over the SALEM product at 62 (nore coolness/\nmenchol taste) reflects the key development need that RGD is working on to\nimprove performance for SALEM.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions.\n\nDd ot peek poutte\ndex Belits pontcok,\n\nMr. E. M. Paul,\nMr. Me Le Suggs\nMs. M. D. Trogdon\n\n82b8 ToZos",
